            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>How to Measure Retention Optimization Effectiveness</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Retention optimization should be measured using a combination of
                    product, customer, and business metrics. The right metrics depend
                    on the product model, customer lifecycle, and specific retention
                    objectives.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Retention Rate:</b> Measure the percentage of customers retained over a defined period.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Churn Rate:</b> Track the percentage of customers who stop using or purchasing the product.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Engagement:</b> Monitor meaningful product usage and customer activity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Feature Adoption:</b> Evaluate whether customers are using important product capabilities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Repeat Usage:</b> Measure how frequently customers return and use the product.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Lifetime Value:</b> Evaluate the long-term value generated by retained customers.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Satisfaction:</b> Use feedback and satisfaction indicators to understand customer experience.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

